\\",\\\"coursesFormula\\\":\\\"run <= ordered length ? 1 : 1 + ceil((run - ordered length) / (ordered length - end lap))\\\",\\\"courses\\\":\\\"1 + ceil((9.81 - 5) / (5 - 0.2)) = 3\\\",\\\"coursesExpanded\\\":\\\"Course 1 covers a full ordered sheet length of 5 m. The remaining 4.81 m is covered by further courses that each add 5 - 0.2 = 4.8 m, so ceil(4.81 / 4.8) = 2 more course(s), giving 3 courses in total.\\\",\\\"courseBoundary\\\":\\\"3 course(s) cover any run greater than 9.8 m and up to and including exactly 14.6 m. A run of 14.600000001 m or more needs 4 courses.\\\",\\\"maxRunAtThisCourseCountM\\\":14.6,\\\"minRunForAnotherCourseM\\\":14.600000001,\\\"wrongFormulaWarning\\\":\\\"Do NOT compute courses as ceil(run / (ordered length - end lap)). It happens to give the correct 3 for this particular input, but it is still the wrong rule and gives a different answer for other runs, because the first course is not shortened by an end lap.\\\",\\\"sheets\\\":\\\"10 columns × 3 courses = 30 sheets\\\",\\\"orderedLength\\\":\\\"30 sheets × 5 m = 150 m\\\",\\\"endLapPolicy\\\":\\\"The first course covers a full ordered sheet length. Each additional course adds ordered length minus end lap.\\\"},\\\"orderedLinearM\\\":150,\\\"coveredWidthM\\\":8,\\\"coveredRunM\\\":14.6,\\\"excessWidthM\\\":0,\\\"excessRunM\\\":4.79,\\\"measurementReference\\\":\\\"QA synthetic 8m by 9.81m developed rectangle (follow-up question)\\\",\\\"supplierReference\\\":\\\"QA supplied effective cover 0.8m ordered length 5m end lap 0.2m\\\",\\\"verifiedQuoteEligible\\\":false,\\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"End lap (the lengthwise lap between courses, also called a transverse lap) IS included in this calculation: every course after the first is shortened by the supplied end lap. Do not describe end laps or transverse laps as excluded.\\\",\\\"Side lap (the lap between adjacent sheets across the width) is NOT calculated here: it is already contained in the supplied effective sheet cover, so it is neither added nor deducted again. Side lap and end lap are separate laps and must be explained separately.\\\",\\\"One rectangular developed surface with identical ordered sheet lengths; no opening deductions, hips, valleys, cutting or reusable offcut schedule.\\\",\\\"No fixings, flashings, product suitability or compliance calculation. References are retained but not validated; draft and not eligible for verified quotes.\\\"]}\",\n          \"images\": 0,\n          \"executionOrigin\": \"model\"\n         },\n         \"id\": \"call_740836aed3bc428590ff587f\"\n        }\n       }\n      ]\n     },\n     {\n      \"role\": \"model\",\n      \"parts\": [\n       {\n        \"text\": \"[xray:withheld-candidate] Not delivered to the user; do not treat as an executed action or a completed answer.\\n# Roof sheet coverage — QA result\\n\\nInputs (supplied): developedWidth 8 m, developedRun 9.8 m, effectiveCover 0.8 m, orderLength 5 m, endLap 0.2 m.\\nReferences: measurement = \\\"QA synthetic 8m by 9.8m developed rectangle\\\"; supplier = \\\"QA supplied effective cover 0.8m ordered length 5m end lap 0.2m\\\".\\n\\n## Tool receipt (9.8 m run)\\n\\n- status: draft-sheet-coverage\\n- columns: 10 (ceil(8 / 0.8))\\n- courses: 2\\n- sheets: 20 (10 × 2)\\n- orderedLinearM: 100 (20 × 5)\\n- coveredRunM: 9.8; excessRunM: 0\\n- verifiedQuoteEligible: false\\n\\nReturned `coursesExpanded`: \\\"Course 1 covers a full ordered sheet length of 5 m. The remaining 4.8 m is covered by further courses that each add 5 − 0.2 = 4.8 m, so ceil(4.8 / 4.8) = 1 more course(s), giving 2 courses in total.\\\"\\n\\nReturned `courseBoundary`: \\\"2 course(s) cover any run greater than 5 m and up to and including exactly 9.8 m. A run of 9.800000001 m or more needs 3 courses.\\\"\\n\\n## How the course count is derived\\n\\nThe store uses:\\n\\n```\\ncourses = run ≤ orderLength ? 1 : 1 + ceil((run - orderLength) / (orderLength - endLap))\\n```\\n\\n- The first course is a full ordered length (5 m) — it is **not** shortened by an end lap.\\n- Every course after the first adds `orderLength − endLap` = 5 − 0.2 = 4.8 m of new run.\\n- For 9.8 m: residual = 4.8 m, ceil(4.8 / 4.8) = 1 → 1 + 1 = **2 courses** (exactly fills 9.8 m).\\n- The store's warning: `ceil(run / (orderLength − endLap))` is **not** the rule; for 9.8 m it would wrongly give 3.\\n\\n## Lap policy (verbatim from the receipt)\\n\\n- **End lap (lengthwise / transverse lap) IS included.** Every course after the first is shortened by the supplied end lap. Do not describe end laps or transverse laps as excluded.\\n- **Side lap (across the width) is NOT separately calculated.** It is already inside the supplied effective sheet cover, so it is neither added nor deducted again. Side lap and end lap are separate laps and must be explained separately.\\n- First-course policy: a full ordered length is laid at the eaves/start ridge; only subsequent courses pay the end lap.\\n\\n## 9.81 m run — follow-up call\\n\\nSame inputs, developedRun `9.81`:\\n\\n- courses: **3** (10 × 3 = 30 sheets; orderedLinearM = 150)\\n- Residual after course 1 = 4.81 m; ceil(4.81 / 4.8) = 2 → 1 + 2 = 3 courses\\n- coveredRunM: 14.6; excessRunM: 4.79 (course 3 lays 5 m, only 4.81 m needed)\\n- Boundary returned: \\\"3 course(s) cover any run greater than 9.8 m and up to and including exactly 14.6 m.\\\"\\n\\nWhy 9.81 m breaks the 2-course plan: the boundary is **strict** at exactly 9.8 m. A residual of 4.81 m does not divide into 4.8 m lengths, so a third 5 m course is required even though the extra run is only 0.01 m. The extra 4.79 m in course 3 is reported as draft excess, not silently trimmed.\\n\\n## Evidence status\\n\\nBoth calls returned `verifiedQuoteEligible: false`. The references are retained from input, not validated. Draft only; not for a verified quote.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Developer review\\n\\n- **Outcome:** Delivered both tool receipts verbatim, explained the first-course-full + end-lap-on-subsequent policy with the exact formula, and contrasted the 9.8 m (2 courses) and 9.81 m (3 courses, excess 4.79 m) cases with the exact boundary numbers the tool returned. Accuracy verified against the store's own `wrongFormulaWarning` caveat.\\n- **Friction:** None material. The instructions explicitly forbade extra reading; both necessary calls were issued in a single parallel block. Required `read_workflow_route` was selected as a static pick, not narrated as project work.\\n- **Improvement:** None specific. Length and structure fit the ask. If a tighter follow-up, the `9.800000001` next-course threshold and the exact excess length for a 9.81 m run could be surfaced as a single sentence earlier in the report — but the current placement is already explicit.\"\n       }\n      ]\n     },\n     {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"parts\": [\n       {\n        \"text\": \"[xray:workflow-check] The workflow is not finished. {\\\"tool\\\":\\\"read_project_context\\\",\\\"args\\\":{},\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Read the current project identity, revision and workspace state.\\\"} Use the required tool and inspect its receipt before a final answer. Do not repeat completed mutations. If an actual tool fails or permission is refused, report that result.\\nThis is an internal completion check, not a new user request. Preserve the original user objective below. After satisfying the required check, return one complete, consolidated answer to that objective, including supported facts from the withheld candidate answer. Do not replace the answer with workflow-selection bookkeeping or a review alone. Correct unsupported claims rather than retaining them.\\nThe current-turn tool outcomes below record only calls from this invocation; earlier transcript receipts are historical, not fresh actions. origin=app-preflight means the app performed a read-only prerequisite, not that the model requested it. invoked=false means the action was not executed. invoked=true records an invocation, not proof that a failed action complete